  "question": {
    "text": "A solid sphere and hollow sphere of the same mass and radius are given a spin about their centre of mass and then, they are placed on a rough horizontal surface. The spin angular velocity is the same for both the spheres and it is equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. Once the pure rolling starts; let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> be the linear speeds of their centres of mass, then"
  },
